    "description": "Agents register as a public OAuth 2.1 client via Dynamic Client Registration (RFC 7591) at register_uri, then send the user through authorization_endpoint (PKCE S256 mandatory) where a human signs in and grants the connection — this consent step is the claim. Exchanging the resulting code at token_endpoint yields an OAuth 2.1 Bearer access token scoped to mcp:access. Agents may instead use a long-lived API key (Bearer zk_...) created at https://zillapi.com/app/keys/. This service does not require or accept ID-JAG identity assertions or a verified-email claim grant; see https://zillapi.com/auth.md for the exact procedure."
